      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Type Transformation Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Types as Functions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Utility type = ==generic type-level function==: type in, new type out",
                "==Erased== at compile time: **zero runtime cost**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Core Set",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Utility",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Partial<T>`",
                  "every property ==optional=="
                ],
                [
                  "`Required<T>`",
                  "strips `?`, all required"
                ],
                [
                  "`Readonly<T>`",
                  "every property `readonly`"
                ],
                [
                  "`Pick<T, K>`",
                  "keeps only keys K"
                ],
                [
                  "`Omit<T, K>`",
                  "drops keys K"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Pick` and `Omit` are built from ==mapped types=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shallow Only",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Partial<User>` does not make nested objects optional",
                "`Readonly<T>` does not freeze nested properties"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type User = { name: string; address: { city: string } };",
                "const u: Readonly<User> = { name: 'A', address: { city: 'X' } };",
                "u.name = 'B';          // error",
                "u.address.city = 'Y';  // allowed"
              ],
              "note": "only the top level is readonly"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Compile time vs runtime",
              "text": "`Readonly<T>` is ==compile-time only==. `Object.freeze` is the **runtime** guard."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Utility Types in Everyday Use",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Utility Types in Everyday Use",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reshaping User",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Partial<User>` as `patch`: ==any subset== of User fields",
                "`Omit<User, 'password'>` ==hides== sensitive fields",
                "`Pick<User, 'id' | 'name'>` ==whitelists== instead"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function update(id: string, patch: Partial<User>) {}",
                "type PublicUser = Omit<User, 'password'>",
                "type Card = Pick<User, 'id' | 'name'>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Record<K, V>",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "`Record<'admin' | 'user', P>`",
                "`Record<string, P>`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Keys",
                  "fixed union",
                  "any string"
                ],
                [
                  "Missing key",
                  "{red:error}, all required",
                  "allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "Shape",
                  "mapped type",
                  "==index signature=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "With ==noUncheckedIndexedAccess==, a lookup returns `P | undefined`",
                "Narrow it first: `if (rec[k]) ...`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The Omit Trap",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Omit<T, K>` has `K extends keyof any`: keys are ==not checked==",
                "A typo compiles and omits ==nothing=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Oops = Omit<User, 'pasword'>",
                "// no error: password is still in Oops"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Omit vs Pick",
              "text": "`Pick` checks its keys against `keyof T`; `Omit` does ==not==. Re-read the resulting type after every Omit."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Function Types: ReturnType, Parameters, infer",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Function Types: ReturnType, Parameters, infer",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Extracting Types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ReturnType<typeof fn>` extracts the return type",
                "Pass `typeof fn`, not `fn`: `ReturnType<fn>` is an {red:error}",
                "`Parameters<typeof fn>` gives the arguments as a ==tuple==",
                "`Parameters<typeof fn>[0]` is the first argument"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Async functions return `Promise<T>`, so unwrap with ==Awaited<...>=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "async function load(id: string) { return user }",
                "type R = ReturnType<typeof load>  // Promise<User>",
                "type U = Awaited<R>  // User"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. infer",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`infer R` declares a type variable inside `extends`",
                "Legal only in the ==extends clause==",
                "It is ==pattern matching== on the type's shape"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type MyReturn<T> = T extends (...args: any[]) => infer R ? R : never"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`ReturnType` is just a conditional type with `infer`"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mapped Types and Conditional Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mapped Types and Conditional Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mapped Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`{ [K in keyof T]: T[K] }` loops over the ==keys of T==",
                "`Partial<T>` = `{ [K in keyof T]?: T[K] }`",
                "`-?` removes optional (`Required<T>`); `-readonly` strips readonly",
                "==as== renames keys; mapping a key to `never` **drops** it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Getters<T> = {",
                " [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]: () => T[K]",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "renames name to getName"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Conditional Types",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`T extends U ? X : Y` picks X or Y",
                "A ==naked== `T` distributes over a union",
                "`type ToArray<T> = T extends any ? T[] : never`",
                "`ToArray<string | number>` gives `string[] | number[]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Union input",
                "Checks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`T extends U`",
                  "{green:distributes}",
                  "each member"
                ],
                [
                  "`[T] extends [U]`",
                  "{red:no distribution}",
                  "whole type"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Testing for never",
              "text": "`never` is an empty union, so a distributive conditional yields ==never==. Use `[T] extends [never]`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "satisfies and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "satisfies and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What satisfies Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==satisfies== (TS 4.9) checks a value against a type",
                "It does ==not widen== the value's inferred type",
                "`red` stays `number[]`, not the union"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const c = {",
                "  red: [255, 0, 0],",
                "  green: \"#0f0\",",
                "} satisfies Record<string, number[] | string>;",
                "c.red.map(n => n / 2);   // number[]",
                "c.green.toUpperCase();   // string"
              ],
              "note": "each property keeps its own type"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Annotation vs satisfies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "const c: T",
                "satisfies T"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Validates",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`c.red` type",
                  "{red:number[] | string}",
                  "{green:number[]}"
                ],
                [
                  "Typo / missing key",
                  "error",
                  "error"
                ],
                [
                  "Exact-key autocomplete",
                  "{red:lost}",
                  "{green:kept}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Typos and missing keys fail ==at the declaration==",
                "Add `as const` for literal, ==readonly== types"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Partial`, `Readonly`, `Required` are ==shallow==: use recursive `DeepPartial<T>`",
                "`Omit` on a union ==collapses== its variants: distribute it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type DeepPartial<T> = {",
                "  [K in keyof T]?: DeepPartial<T[K]>;",
                "};",
                "type DistOmit<T, K extends keyof any> =",
                "  T extends any ? Omit<T, K> : never;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Annotation ==widens==; satisfies ==validates and keeps== the exact type."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Utility and Advanced Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Utility and Advanced Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Utility Types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Partial<T>`",
                  "all optional"
                ],
                [
                  "`Required<T>`",
                  "all required"
                ],
                [
                  "`Readonly<T>`",
                  "all readonly"
                ],
                [
                  "`Pick<T, 'a' | 'b'>`",
                  "keeps those keys"
                ],
                [
                  "`Omit<T, 'a'>`",
                  "drops keys"
                ],
                [
                  "`Record<K, V>`",
                  "object from key union"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Modifiers are all ==shallow==",
                "`Omit` never checks keys: a typo omits nothing"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Function Extraction",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pass `typeof f`, not `f`",
                "`Awaited` unwraps the Promise"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type R = ReturnType<typeof f>",
                "type P = Parameters<typeof f>",
                "type A = Awaited<ReturnType<typeof g>>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mapped, Conditional, satisfies",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`+`/`-` add or strip `readonly` and `?`",
                "`T extends U ? X : Y`; `infer R` captures a type",
                "Naked `T` ==distributes== over unions",
                "`[T] extends [U]` does not distribute",
                "`satisfies` validates without widening"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type M<T> = {",
                "  -readonly [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]-?: T[K]",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "mapped template"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Shallow",
              "text": "Nested objects stay untouched; write a recursive `DeepPartial<T>`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`type A = Omit<{ id: number; name: string }, 'nme'>` compiles. What is A?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Still `{ id: number; name: string }`",
                "Omit does not check that K is a key of T, so the typo drops nothing"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`type A<T> = T extends unknown ? T[] : never` and `type B<T> = [T] extends [unknown] ? T[] : never`. What are A and B for `string | number`?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "A gives `string[] | number[]`, because a naked T distributes over the union",
                "B gives `(string | number)[]`, because the tuple wrap stops distribution"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`const c = { red: [255,0,0] } satisfies Record<string, number[] | string>`. Does `c.red.map(...)` compile? What if you write `const c: Record<string, number[] | string> = ...` instead?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "With satisfies, yes: red stays `number[]`",
                "With the annotation, no: red widens to `number[] | string`, and `.map` doesn't exist on string"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
